  "seed_strategy": "gen_seeds writes exactly two deterministic valid files per operation. For lz4_block_roundtrip and lz4_hc_block_roundtrip, it writes two distinct realistic plaintext payloads: one text-heavy log/JSON-like corpus with repeated keys/records and one binary-ish structured corpus made from repeated headers, small counters, and recurring substrings to ensure compressibility and dictionary hits. For lz4_frame_decompress, it first synthesizes those same two large realistic plaintext buffers, then uses LZ4F_compressFrame to encode each into a valid frame blob and writes the resulting compressed bytes as the seeds. For xxhash_streaming, it reuses two distinct realistic raw payloads. gen_perf emits large multi-megabyte inputs only for the scaling ops: raw realistic plaintext for the two block round-trip ops, a large valid frame produced by LZ4F_compressFrame for lz4_frame_decompress, and a large realistic raw buffer for xxhash_streaming. All bytes are deterministic and generated without randomness."
